/-! # Actual scaled-root support and removable scale charts

The current closure supplies uniform root bounds and sector directions on
the discount half-plane, both spatial root signs from actual ladder
identities, genuine scale-zero extensions of the actual roots, all-order
scale jets and Taylor remainders, their Brownian zero values, and the actual scaled marked denominator
with its uniformly invertible holomorphic unit. The unmarked denominator,
real-drift canonical Taylor surrogates and their true-factor exponential
errors, and the actual quadratic quotient along the scale roots now carry
uniform holomorphic and Taylor budgets as well. Complex-scale sectors,
first-order surrogate ratio budgets and quantitative denominator bounds
are now paid. A genuine spatial divided difference gives a nonzero
holomorphic denominator also at the joint origin.
The regular surrogate bridge is identified with the actual normal bridge
after real scaling and has pointwise complex-scale Taylor budgets.
The individual complex-scale roots now retain the correct decay direction
with the scaled width. Negative-drift bridge norms have class-uniform
polynomial exponential envelopes and decaying scale Taylor budgets.
Positive-drift half-line subtraction now has a polynomial exponential
envelope and decaying Taylor budgets, with exact physical normal-form
identification. A reciprocal polynomial common radius gives genuinely
drift-integrable all-order Taylor envelopes. The removable surrogate
entrance has joint scale-spatial holomorphy and exact physical scaling
across all collisions. Weighted spatial slopes and their inverse retain
the endpoint exponential factors. Cubic combinations absorb the scaled
marker on a reciprocal polynomial disc. The negative-drift entrance-square
bridge amplitude now has drift-integrable all-order Taylor envelopes.
Half-line entrance subtraction has an exact first-slope formula retaining
positive-root marker collisions. The central drift interval and positive
half-line subtraction now complete the amplitude bounds on every real
scaled drift, with a unified integrable all-order Taylor envelope.
True marked and unmarked endpoint limits now agree after physical scaling.
The zero-discount endpoint has true all-order surrogate Taylor remainders
and finite X8 jet determination. The marked zero derivative equals minus
the same finite endpoint. True-factor complete-pair errors on imaginary frequencies now retain a
polynomial exponential integrable envelope; the unmarked endpoint
nonzero-discount extension remains open.
The actual bridge now has weighted true-versus-surrogate errors, supported
by a frequency-uniform divided-denominator relative error and an actual
nonzero denominator disc independent of the requested Taylor order.
The actual entrance now has complete weighted surrogate errors. Both new
actual forms are identified with their physical canonical regular forms
and agree exactly with every surrogate at zero scale. Their physical scaling
identities extend to the full canonical discount disc. The actual bridge
frequency derivative is identified with the fixed physical discount
derivative. The full actual pair retains both time-operator terms, has the
exact cubic physical scaling and agrees with each surrogate at zero scale.
Complete actual-versus-surrogate pair errors now retain both operator
terms and the positive-tail half-line cancellation on imaginary frequencies.
The marked endpoint now has exact pole cancellation, a fixed actual disc
independent of the Taylor order, square-root frequency decay, all-order
real-scale surrogate Taylor errors, and a continuous Brownian scale-zero
limit depending only on the actual variance. Its physical identification
includes zero mark, and its zero-mark derivative agrees with the true
finite endpoint. Unmarked endpoint budgets and kernel jet determination
remain open. Locally even square-root descent now has a derivative formula
without a root denominator and all-order Cauchy budgets; the complete pair
has an actual complete-pair instantiation at zero drift.
The actual bridge is holomorphic on a class-controlled common complex
frequency disc through the imaginary axis and root mergers. Its all-order
frequency derivative bounds retain the physical root-size gain and hence
have no negative scale powers. These are polynomial coarse budgets; the
negative-drift complete actual pair now has an exponential derivative
budget and a cubic polynomial drift-integrable envelope on the imaginary
frequency axis. Its actual scale disc is independent of the requested
Taylor order and no negative scale powers remain. The positive-tail
half-line bridge and its correction now have a common full frequency disc;
rightward differences pay correction derivative decay. The actual entrance
correction retains the negative-root exponential weight. Both terms of the
complete time operator give positive-tail half-line pair cancellation.
Central-drift decay completes a single cubic polynomial exponential
envelope on every real drift. The envelope is drift-integrable. Actual real-drift root, quotient, canonical
factor and moving divided-slope continuity now pay measurability of the
complete time operator by rightward difference quotients. The fixed-cutoff
actual subtracted complete pair is genuinely Bochner integrable under the
same second-order Sobolev assumptions, including root mergers.
The half-line components are identified on the full canonical discount
disc, their fixed physical discount derivative is paid, and the subtracted
complete pair has the exact cubic physical scaling. All-drift pair errors
remain open. The complete surrogate now has local joint scale-frequency
holomorphy on every real drift through the imaginary axis, including the
joint origin, and all frequency jets are jointly holomorphic on one
local neighborhood.
The removable signed Morse chart is now jointly holomorphic in scale and
coordinate, and its exact actual-root identification includes zero scale.
Individual actual roots are jointly holomorphic in scale and frequency
away from the joint drift-frequency origin, on a class-controlled radius.
At zero drift the actual lifted spatial family, divided denominator and
second divided numerator are jointly holomorphic and even in the signed
coordinate. A nonzero denominator and square-root descent pay the complete
pair and every actual frequency jet through the joint origin, including
zero scale, on one local neighborhood independent of the Taylor order.
At zero real drift the actual complete pair equals every surrogate.
Outside the joint origin actual open signed-root charts, branch-independent
quotient identification, spatial continuity and holomorphic slices pay the
complete surrogate entrance, bridge, frequency derivative and time-operator
pair. A positive class-controlled scale radius covers every real drift;
local frequency neighborhoods still depend on the center and law.
Actual real-drift canonical Taylor errors now retain their drift vanishing
order under every discount-spatial mixed derivative. Actual moving-root
frequency derivative errors, divided-denominator errors and inverse errors
retain endpoint exponentials and first or second drift weights. The actual
frequency radius is independent of the surrogate order; approximation
slopes additionally use the requested-order surrogate domain. Complete
bridge and positive-tail correction derivative errors and both complete
time-operator errors now retain their endpoint exponentials. A higher
surrogate degree absorbs the drift weights without inverse drift or scale
powers, including exact zero-drift agreement. Complete subtracted-pair
errors on all real drifts now have b^(N+2) times degree N+5 polynomial
exponential envelopes, including entrance-square and half-line errors.
Approximation slopes use the requested-order domain; complex-scale
complete-pair Taylor budgets and coefficient identification remain open. Moving divided differences now support several
complex parameters using joint continuity and actual holomorphic slices.
A fixed physical drift cutoff now pays the actual decay disc independently
of Taylor order. The resulting endpoint-minus-pair expression has a
square-root frequency bound on the full mid scale, with a cubic frequency
polynomial. The actual cutoff kernel is now measurable and integrable. An explicit
order-dependent approximation cutoff preserves the fixed actual physical
cutoff. Complete surrogate time-operator derivatives are measurable; both
cutoff kernels are genuinely Bochner integrable and their integral error
is bounded by b^(N+2) times a degree N+5 square-root-frequency polynomial
with exponential frequency decay. The central signed-root quotient is jointly continuous with holomorphic
parameter/spatial slices. Explicit class-controlled root and scale discs
pay a uniform nonzero divided denominator through root merging. Even
square-root descent gives a jointly holomorphic frequency continuation
and a uniform actual frequency derivative bound, identified with the
original surrogate on the right half-plane through zero scale. The
complete central time-operator pair now has a uniform complex-scale
bound, all scale jets and arbitrary-order Taylor remainders. These
central drift and frequency radii depend on the requested surrogate
order and class constants, and are chosen before the law. The outer
frequency region and positive-tail subtraction still require complete
pair Taylor budgets. Identification with the normal transform and its
class-independent assembly remain open.
-/
